On Sun, Nov 28, 2010 at 11:09 AM, Oren <get.oren@gmail.com> wrote:
> How about:
> L1 { lo djacu ku dunja lo jacke'o be li no vau ja'a xu }

That's not grammatical. Because of a quirk in the grammar, in the term
"ja'a ku" the "ku" is not elidable, and also "vau" says that there are
no more terms for this bridi-tail, so you can't follow it with another
term. But this would be grammatical:

  lo djacu cu dunja lo jacke'o be li no ja'a ku xu

mu'o mi'e xorxes

